---
title: Map
layout: base.njk
map: true
# LOCAL ONLY. The permalink is decided in src/map.11tydata.js, which returns
# false on a Cloudflare build — so this page is not written, not linked and
# not deployed. It exists at http://localhost:8080/map/ under `npm run dev`
# and nowhere else.
#
# To publish it when it is ready: add `navLabel: map` and `navOrder: 3` here,
# then follow the note in src/map.11tydata.js.
noindex: true
description: Where every*one is happening — every venue in the Adelaide Design Week 2026 program, on one map of Kaurna/Adelaide.
---

<header class="pg-head map-head">
<h1 class="pg-h1">Map</h1>
<p class="pg-intro">{{ mapPoints.eventCount }} events across {{ mapPoints.venueCount }} places. Tap an <svg class="ast ast--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ast"></use></svg> to see what is on there.</p>
</header>

{% if env.mapboxToken %}

<div class="map-wrap">

  {# Mapbox GL draws its markers to a canvas: they cannot be tabbed to and a
     screen reader sees nothing. This list opens the same panel the markers
     do, and is the only way in without a mouse. #}
  <nav id="adw-map-venues" class="map-venues visually-hidden" aria-label="All venues">
    <h2>All venues</h2>
    <ul>
      {%- for v in mapPoints.venues %}
      <li><button type="button" data-venue="{{ v.slug }}">{{ v.venue }} — {{ v.count }} event{% if v.count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</button></li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <div id="adw-map" class="map-canvas" role="application" aria-label="Map of Adelaide Design Week venues"></div>

  <aside id="adw-map-panel" class="map-panel" hidden aria-label="Venue details">
    <button type="button" class="map-panel-close" aria-label="Close venue details">close</button>
    <div class="map-panel-body"></div>
  </aside>

</div>

<div class="map-legend">
  <h2 class="map-legend-h">the marks</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-exh" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> exhibition</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-conv" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> conversation</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-inst" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> installation</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-open" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> open studio</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-tour" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> tour</li>
    <li><span class="lg-mark lg-work" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ast"><use href="#ast"></use></svg></span> workshop</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="map-legend-note">A bigger <svg class="ast ast--sm" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#ast"></use></svg> with a number is several events together — tap it to open them up.</p>
</div>

{# Parsed by map.js. A script tag of type application/json is inert: the
   browser never executes it, so event titles and blurbs cannot escape into
   the page as code. #}
<script type="application/json" id="adw-map-data">{{ { "token": env.mapboxToken, "style": site.mapboxStyle, "geojson": mapPoints.geojson } | dump | safe }}</script>

{% else %}

<div class="page prose">
  <p><strong>The map is not switched on yet.</strong> Copy <code>.env.example</code> to <code>.env</code> and put a public Mapbox token (<code>pk.</code>) in <code>MAPBOX_PUBLIC_TOKEN</code>, then restart <code>npm run dev</code>.</p>
</div>

{% endif %}

{% if mapPoints.dropped.length %}
{# Visible to editors reading the page source, not to visitors. A venue that
   quietly fails to appear is the failure mode worth making noisy. #}
<!--
  Not on the map ({{ mapPoints.dropped.length }}):
  {%- for d in mapPoints.dropped %}
  - {{ d.title }} @ {{ d.venue }} — {{ d.reason }}
  {%- endfor %}
-->
{% endif %}
